 - Resume boundary
   - Because call frames add new durable lineage and resume keys, resume from pre-`schema_version: "2.1"` state is rejected unless a tested upgrader ships with the same tranche.
 
+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+State schema stays `2.1`; the profile is an additive, optional top-level
+`result_persistence_profile` field.
+
+- Selector
+  - Absent means the historical bundle-backed persistence; `to_dict()` omits the
+    key and a payload without it loads as `None` and round-trips unchanged.
+  - The only supported value is `derived_pure_replay.v1`. Any other present value
+    fails closed with a `ValueError` naming the profile at `RunState`
+    construction, at `StateManager.initialize(...)` and on load; a failed load
+    leaves the state file byte-for-byte unchanged.
+  - `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=None)` writes the
+    field atomically with the new state, before any visit. Ordinary loads never
+    infer, backfill or upgrade it.
+  - Automatic selection: a successfully compiled public `.orc` run, a new root
+    created by `orchestrator resume --force-restart` (the source run stays
+    byte-for-byte unchanged; the new root keeps the requested observability
+    settings), and a fresh non-iterative child call frame whose callee bundle has
+    validated provenance `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"` (a fresh retry after a
+    failed non-iterative Workflow Lisp predecessor is new state). Selection comes
+    from the callee's typed provenance, never from the parent's profile, a path
+    suffix, an alias or a step identity. Existing roots/frames, non-Workflow-Lisp
+    callees and iteration-owned frames keep the historical profile; an existing
+    frame is never backfilled, and one with no mapping `state` is rejected with a
+    `ValueError` ("existing call-frame state") before anything is written.
+
+- Eligibility
+  - A compiler-generated `pure_projection` is replay-eligible when it is acyclic
+    and visited at most once per scope (not loop-owned, not on a control-flow
+    cycle, no `publishes`). Others keep full durable rows, bundles and
+    checkpoints inside a profiled run. The index is derived from the loaded
+    bundle (`orchestrator.workflow.pure_result_replay.derive_pure_result_replay_index`)
+    and never changes the serialized runtime plan. Refs are scoped to the workflow
+    holding them; only exact `{"ref": ...}` leaves form dependency edges and every
+    literal subtree must match its declared binding type.
+
+- Value-free completion shell
+  - A successful eligible visit persists exactly
+    `{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0,
+    "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed",
+    "retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}`; any extra,
+    missing or different key is invalid. Failed and skipped rows stay full rows,
+    and a skip or pre-visit failure of an eligible node still records its single
+    visit.
+  - Each of `begin_eligible_pure_visit`, `settle_eligible_pure_success` and
+    `settle_eligible_pure_failure` is one atomic state transaction; the running
+    cursor carries the visit count and step identity. Progress classifies as
+    `unstarted`, `interrupted`, `derived_complete`, `durable_failure_skip`, or
+    fails with `progress_witness_invalid` (visit two, mismatched cursor/row,
+    value-bearing completion, ...).
+
+- Resume
+  - Resume validates only the dependency leaves the restart boundary needs (bound
+    inputs, durable effect rows and intrinsics), re-derives the needed pure values
+    in memory over an overlay and never dispatches effects, increments visits,
+    settles results or writes durable state. It fails closed before any effect
+    with `error.type == "pure_result_replay_unavailable"` and
+    `error.context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`,
+    `binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`,
+    `progress_witness_invalid`, `dependency_index_invalid`,
+    `reachability_ambiguous`, `multiple_visit_region`, `profile_conflict`.
+  - A persisted value row, pure result bundle or private-lineage entry for an
+    eligible node, or an eligible node's checkpoint record or restore binding in
+    the same scope, is a `profile_conflict` (`context.surface` is `steps`,
+    `pure_bundle`, `private_artifact_versions`, `checkpoint_record` or
+    `restore_payload`), raised before the prologue or any state write.
+  - The restart boundary is determined once per resume and passed to the
+    default-resume decision.
+
+- Checkpoints
+  - Eligible pure points emit no checkpoint record and are filtered from the
+    durable candidates before unique-nearest selection (selection never scans past
+    an invalid nearest durable boundary). Restore payloads omit bindings sourced
+    from eligible pure steps. Default resume admits exactly one zero-record case,
+    `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY` (`selection_reason`
+    `validated_frame_entry_replay`, null `checkpoint_id`), when validated
+    bound-input leaves and exact profile/progress witnesses exist; otherwise it
+    fails closed with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`.
+
 ## State File Schema (example)
 
 The state file (`${RUN_ROOT}/state.json`) is the authoritative record of execution:
